#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "scalar(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:7
msgid "scalar - A tool for managing large Git repositories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"scalar clone [--single-branch] [--branch <main-branch>] [--full-clone]\n"
"\t[--[no-]src] [--[no-]tags] [--[no-]maintenance] <url> [<enlistment>]\n"
"scalar list\n"
"scalar register [--[no-]maintenance] [<enlistment>]\n"
"scalar unregister [<enlistment>]\n"
"scalar run ( all | config | commit-graph | fetch | loose-objects | "
"pack-files ) [<enlistment>]\n"
"scalar reconfigure [--maintenance=(enable|disable|keep)] [ --all | "
"<enlistment> ]\n"
"scalar diagnose [<enlistment>]\n"
"scalar delete <enlistment>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Scalar is a repository management tool that optimizes Git for use in large "
"repositories. Scalar improves performance by configuring advanced Git "
"settings, maintaining repositories in the background, and helping to reduce "
"data sent across the network."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:35
msgid ""
"An important Scalar concept is the enlistment: this is the top-level "
"directory of the project. It usually contains the subdirectory `src/` which "
"is a Git worktree. This encourages the separation between tracked files "
"(inside `src/`)  and untracked files, such as build artifacts (outside "
"`src/`). When registering an existing Git worktree with Scalar whose name is "
"not `src`, the enlistment will be identical to the worktree."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:39
msgid ""
"The `scalar` command implements various subcommands, and different options "
"depending on the subcommand. With the exception of `clone`, `list` and "
"`reconfigure --all`, all subcommands expect to be run in an enlistment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:41
msgid "The following options can be specified _before_ the subcommand:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-C <directory>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:45
msgid ""
"Before running the subcommand, change the working directory. This option "
"imitates the same option of linkgit:git[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-c <key>=<value>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:49
msgid ""
"For the duration of running the specified subcommand, configure this "
"setting. This option imitates the same option of linkgit:git[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "COMMANDS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clone"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "clone [<options>] <url> [<enlistment>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Clones the specified repository, similar to linkgit:git-clone[1]. By "
"default, only commit and tree objects are cloned. Once finished, the "
"worktree is located at `<enlistment>/src`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:68
msgid ""
"The sparse-checkout feature is enabled (except when run with `--full-clone`)  "
"and the only files present are those in the top-level directory. Use `git "
"sparse-checkout set` to expand the set of directories you want to see, or "
"`git sparse-checkout disable` to expand to all files (see "
"linkgit:git-sparse-checkout[1] for more details). You can explore the "
"subdirectories outside your sparse-checkout by using `git ls-tree "
"HEAD[:<directory>]`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-b <name>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--branch <name>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:73
msgid ""
"Instead of checking out the branch pointed to by the cloned repository's "
"HEAD, check out the `<name>` branch instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--single-branch`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-single-branch`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:79
msgid ""
"Clone only the history leading to the tip of a single branch, either "
"specified by the `--branch` option or the primary branch remote's `HEAD` "
"points at."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:84
msgid ""
"Further fetches into the resulting repository will only update the "
"remote-tracking branch for the branch this option was used for the initial "
"cloning. If the HEAD at the remote did not point at any branch when "
"`--single-branch` clone was made, no remote-tracking branch is created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--src`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-src`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:90
msgid ""
"By default, `scalar clone` places the cloned repository within a "
"`<entlistment>/src` directory. Use `--no-src` to place the cloned repository "
"directly in the `<enlistment>` directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--tags`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-tags`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:98
msgid ""
"By default, `scalar clone` will fetch the tag objects advertised by the "
"remote and future `git fetch` commands will do the same. Use `--no-tags` to "
"avoid fetching tags in `scalar clone` and to configure the repository to "
"avoid fetching tags in the future. To fetch tags after cloning with "
"`--no-tags`, run `git fetch --tags`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--full-clone`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-full-clone`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:103
msgid ""
"A sparse-checkout is initialized by default. This behavior can be turned off "
"via `--full-clone`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:104
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--maintenance`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:105
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-maintenance`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:109
msgid ""
"By default, `scalar clone` configures the enlistment to use Git's background "
"maintenance feature. Use the `--no-maintenance` to skip this configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "List"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "list"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:116
msgid ""
"List enlistments that are currently registered by Scalar. This subcommand "
"does not need to be run inside an enlistment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "Register"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "register [<enlistment>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:125
msgid ""
"Adds the enlistment's repository to the list of registered repositories and "
"starts background maintenance. If `<enlistment>` is not provided, then the "
"enlistment associated with the current working directory is registered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:129
msgid ""
"Note: when this subcommand is called in a worktree that is called `src/`, "
"its parent directory is considered to be the Scalar enlistment. If the "
"worktree is _not_ called `src/`, it itself will be considered to be the "
"Scalar enlistment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:136
msgid ""
"By default, `scalar register` configures the enlistment to use Git's "
"background maintenance feature. Use the `--no-maintenance` to skip this "
"configuration. This does not disable any maintenance that may already be "
"enabled in other ways."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:138
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unregister"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:140
#, no-wrap
msgid "unregister [<enlistment>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:143
msgid ""
"Remove the specified repository from the list of repositories registered "
"with Scalar and stop the scheduled background maintenance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"scalar run ( all | config | commit-graph | fetch | loose-objects | "
"pack-files ) [<enlistment>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:152
msgid ""
"Run the given maintenance task (or all tasks, if `all` was specified).  "
"Except for `all` and `config`, this subcommand simply hands off to "
"linkgit:git-maintenance[1] (mapping `fetch` to `prefetch` and `pack-files` "
"to `incremental-repack`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:156
msgid ""
"These tasks are run automatically as part of the scheduled maintenance, as "
"soon as the repository is registered with Scalar. It should therefore not be "
"necessary to run this subcommand manually."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:161
msgid ""
"The `config` task is specific to Scalar and configures all those opinionated "
"default settings that make Git work more efficiently with large "
"repositories. As this task is run as part of `scalar clone` automatically, "
"explicit invocations of this task are rarely needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconfigure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:168
msgid ""
"After a Scalar upgrade, or when the configuration of a Scalar enlistment was "
"somehow corrupted or changed by mistake, this subcommand allows to "
"reconfigure the enlistment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:169
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--all`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:173
msgid ""
"When `--all` is specified, reconfigure all enlistments currently registered "
"with Scalar by the `scalar.repo` config key. Use this option after each "
"upgrade to get the latest features."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:174
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--maintenance=(enable|disable|keep)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:181
msgid ""
"By default, Scalar configures the enlistment to use Git's background "
"maintenance feature; this is the same as using the `enable` value for this "
"option. Use the\t`disable` value to remove each considered enlistment from "
"background maintenance.  Use `keep' to leave the background maintenance "
"configuration untouched for these repositories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagnose"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:185
#, no-wrap
msgid "diagnose [<enlistment>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:189
msgid ""
"When reporting issues with Scalar, it is often helpful to provide the "
"information gathered by this command, including logs and certain statistics "
"describing the data shape of the current enlistment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:192
msgid ""
"The output of this command is a `.zip` file that is written into a directory "
"adjacent to the worktree in the `src` directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "Delete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "delete <enlistment>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/scalar.adoc:199
msgid ""
"This subcommand lets you delete an existing Scalar enlistment from your "
"local file system, unregistering the repository."
msgstr ""

